A||||19||Leadfoot||Some people just don't get it!||||8||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||09-27-2001||09:38 PM||||So I pull into work this morning and I notice a sweet brand new Z06 Corvette parked all the way at the end of the parking lot.  I decided to park near it, like 5 car spaces away from it since the guy/gal obviously parked it far away so no one would bump it with their doors.  As I am getting out I hear this POS import 4 banger (but running on only 3) heading towards me.  It was a mitsumazda something or other which was severely rusted.  The owner decided to park it right next to the Z06 and was so close that he could barely get out.  WTF There is like 30 other places to park and he had to pick the one right next to the Z.  I tell you some people just don't have a clue.   ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Tina||09-27-2001||09:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR><B> I tell you some people just don't have a clue.   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Funny that you brought that up.<BR>Just got back from the store.<P>Yes, I'am one of those people who parks far away from other cars.<P>Anyways, standing in the checkout when I hear the alarm go off on mine.<BR>Some stupid truck JUST HAD to park next to me, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> but no mayor security breach.<BR>2 minutes later I walk out of the store,truck is now parked on the other side.<BR>Betcha, he couldn't hear his cell with all the bells and whistles going off on the Fiero.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||thomas_l||09-28-2001||09:38 AM||||I only park really close to the cars that are so special as to take up two good spaces instead of one in the back 40. If you're that worried about parking lots you need to keep that sucker locked in the garage sealed in a ziplock bag or something.||||reg||13
Z||000003||Fformula88||09-28-2001||10:09 AM||||For every one person who wants to keep their car nice and parks it far away from all the other parked cars, there are 10 people looking to be the first to put that first new scratch/ding/dent into the side!  I parked at wall mart the other day off to the side.  Was the ONLy car in the whole row!!  When I came out... there was a car right on top of mine!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  His passenger side was up against my drivers door so I think I was saved a new scratch... but it wasn't fun trying to get into my car!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hartz||09-28-2001||10:54 AM||||People do it just to be mean.  The trick is to not make your car stand out, but still protect it as much as possible.  The guy parked sideways across three spaces 100 feet from nowhere is just asking for trouble.  Don't draw attention to yourself.  Find a nice end spot, preferrably where the exposed side of the car is to the passenger's side of the next car.  Stay within the lines, but shy to the far side of the parking spot.  Try to park under lights if at night.  And in general - be thankful our cars are plastic and don't show door dings easily!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>home.mindspring.com/~hartzfeld||||reg||1
Z||000005||LarryB||09-28-2001||02:26 PM||||People that pull those stunts know exactly what they're doing, they are just being mean-spirited.<P>I don't give a rats butt if someone does that in the back 40, it's pretty much the same deal as an 18 wheeler parking way out in nowhereland so they don't bother anyone else.<BR>It's when they do it right near the building that annoys me.  Funny though, it's usually not Saab or BMW owners that do this. <P>We had one jerk once that parked his Mustang's passenger side up against the drivers side of my friend's new Camaro so he'd have to crawl over from the passenger side door.  So I just did the same thing to him and tipped off my friend what the dealio was.<P>This little twerp was all bent out of shape when he went to leave work, couldn't get into his car, and we both had conveniently vanished elsewhere in the building.  He never pulled that crap again though. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by thomas_l:<BR><B>I only park really close to the cars that are so special as to take up two good spaces instead of one in the back 40. If you're that worried about parking lots you need to keep that sucker locked in the garage sealed in a ziplock bag or something.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||09-28-2001||02:43 PM||||I hate it when idiots park so close you can't even get into your car! As for parking "out of the way", I can respect that someone wants some "space" around their car. I have many "dings" in my daily driver from people at work. Since I only use the car to go to and from work it's obvious where it is happening. I usually park next to people I know.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/oreif1.jpg">     <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||09-28-2001||03:18 PM||||Where I work, my friends and I usually park in the back row of the parking log, in one space, but we leave a space between our cars.  Since the lot is rarely full, no one usually parks between us.  But every once in a while, someone will go out of their way to park between us, even then there are empty spaces closer to the building with no cars around them!  Go figure.||||reg||6
Z||000008||Brandon86SE||09-28-2001||04:06 PM||||I don't know if it happens to anyone else, but I have a feeling the people who drive the big trucks are out to get me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I typically park out of the way, I don't mind walking an extra minute if it means my car will be out of everyone else's way.  I don't double park, unless say I'm picking up a friend at work after it's closed, and the lot is empty, or something like that.  But what *often* happens to me is that I'll get a couple of massive trucks, or vans on either side of me!<P>Once I was at the mall, parked nearly in the far back corner.  I just had to run in and get my glasses adjusted.  When I got out there were Ford F-350's on either side of me!  Same company logo, and everything.  There were dozens of other spots WAY closer to the entrance.  I had to pray that no cars were coming while backing out, 'cause I couldn't see a damn thing!  Since this time, I've taken to backing into parking spaces, but it's still annoying.  The same kind of thing often happens at school.  grr....  Guess they're all jealous, or something.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||starfighter007@msn.com||09-28-2001||05:34 PM||||I always try to park far away from everybody to keep my cars from gettig dings in them.Now my wife on the other hand looks for the closest parking spot to the entrance.along with everybody else. The only thing that she ever worrys about is starting the car up and going.Idiot lights dont bother her either. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Ken Wittlief||09-28-2001||09:13 PM||||I got to chime in on this one<P>it seems to be the guys that are so stuck on their car that they have to park it at the end of the lot, and still take up 4 spaces, and usually its some repainted old POS<P> is he really worried about someone smacking it? or does he want to make sure EVERYONE can see it while its there? Or does he want to oggle his own car as he walks back towards it across the looooonnngg parking lot?<P> Or is this someway of demonstrating to the girl with him "my car is more important than you - you can walk" ?!<P> these are the same guys who place an ad in the swap sheet or paper, with the words "no dreamers" at the end of the ad. (Yeah right, like half the people in town dream of owning your car).<P> when I see this, one word comes to mind - trailertrash!<P> real class is the guy with the new vette, porche, or M-benz who parks right along with the other cars in the lot.<P>  Its not what you have - its how you spend it. If someone bangs their door into your $80,000 car, and you glance over, shrug and wave them off with a casual "no big deal -Ill have Fritz rub it out next time I take it in"<P>  to me, thats class, thats wealth, thats a person with a quiet soul inside. If you have a real jewel of a machine there, and its NOT the most important thing in the world to you - then you must have a LOT of other great things in your life too.||||reg||10
Z||000011||thomas_l||09-29-2001||08:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>to me, thats class, thats wealth, thats a person with a quiet soul inside. If you have a real jewel of a machine there, and its NOT the most important thing in the world to you - then you must have a LOT of other great things in your life too.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Couldn't have said it better. I sure didn't on my earlier post  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. If I had a special, show quality (read: not just new car, new paint, etc) I would be anal enough not to park in public lots unless it was a car show. And it would live in my garage 99% of the time. My daily drivers are a '00 Lincoln LS and a '01 MB C240. Not necessarily $80k worth (well maybe if stacked on top of each other at the dealership when brand new  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">). I park with the rest of the mob. I will avoid those GD tempting spaces with a long pickup bed crowding in but I'm OK as long as there's enough room to get in/out. I want my nearly new cars to look good, but I also know that they won't be new forever. The Mercedes deal is extra-cool. At lease end, any flaw smaller than a credit card (~2" X 3" not the credit limit) doesn't get charged to you. I went to a Mercedes tent event and watched a MB Credit guy demonstrate on a used E-class with a ball peen hammer. I don't plan to do any demos on mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The ones that need a boot to the head are those that crowd a space because they are too stupid or lazy to park straight between the lines, or the ones that drive through into the opposing side for that "backed-in" look and leave two feet of ass in the empty space behind them.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Phil||09-29-2001||08:32 AM||||About the only time the parking space prima donna gets to me is the diagonal double space taker upper. Also have to add those proximity alarm systems- you know the ones that have a voice and say " You are too close to this car please move away"<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ken Wittlief||09-29-2001||10:21 AM||||proximity alarms is why God invented spit!<P>any car that mouths off to me gets baptised.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tina||09-29-2001||10:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by starfighter007@msn.com:<BR><B>Now my wife on the other hand looks for the closest parking spot to the entrance, along with everybody else. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Seems pretty common around here too, these<BR>"Parking lot pile up's".<BR>Myself I don't get it.<BR>The time it takes to wait for the car to pull out and for you to pull in, or driving around in cirles for the first 5 or 10 in the lot<BR>....by that time I'am walking passed you.<BR>(Nice side effect... less dings.<BR>Especially when you gotta rub the dings out yourself... due to the lack of "a Fritz" on standby)<P>Tina||||reg||1
